==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dark Summoner Satoru''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Devil Hunter Satoru''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Satoru is an excellent Aku crowd-controller with high ability uptime and guaranteed effect. Combined with his decent survivability and good standing range, he can easily counter most Aku enemies, especially Aku backliners which are typically the most problematic of all. Satoru also has immunity to [[Surge Attack|Surges]] to protect himself from any that happen to spawn on him.

However, Satoru suffers as an Aku crowd-controller due to his low Shield Piercing Chance of 20% in spite of his very slow attack rate. This greatly limits his utility despite his wide area of effect, as he is forced to rely on other units to get past Shields that block all status effects, and if they don't succeed, Aku threats can simply ignore his presence.

==='''True Form'''===
Satoru's True Form fixes many of the issues he used to have. The biggest one is Shield Piercing, going from a low 20% to a good 50%. This makes it more likely to Slow and Knockback Aku, greatly enhancing his viability against them. Speaking of Knockback, it is another great help to his kit as an anti-Aku Uber. While the combination of Slow and Knockback initially seems concerning due to the fact it can push backliners together with melee enemies causing your attackers to come into their range kill them, thanks to Satoru's great piercing range of up to 770, this is a non-issue and instead helps by pushing enemies away from his blindspot. A small health bonus is a good quality as he can take a few more hits, but otherwise isn't too noteworthy.

Overall, Satoru's True Form greatly enhances his anti-Aku capabilities and is a great choice for nearly every Aku stage, and will be a fantastic unit during Aku Realms.

==='''Talents'''===
'''Survive''' as a Talent on an anti-Aku can be situational, but ultimately allows him more flexibility given his abysmal HP. Despite the incredibly aggressive nature of Aku enemies, Satoru can find opportunity to reposition in situations which would usually put him in the grave. The only thing holding this Talent back is Satoru's long foreswing animation which can lead to him being juggled regardless.

'''Curse Immunity''' is not something worth investing in. The only Aku that curses is [[Malevolent Dark Cat]], who can and will tear him to pieces in seconds, making it irrelevant. As for Aku/Relic mixed stages, [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] can cover that for the most part. Even if one doesn't own Uril, this Talent finds little utility regardless thanks to Satoru's foreswing animation giving him enough time for the effect to wear off entirely before he attacks.

'''Knockback Immune''' is the least useful Talent of the group. Should any knockback enemies actually make their way to Satoru, the most likely scenario is that other Aku enemies would have reached him as well, spelling his doom. What's more, his health is low enough to where most attacks stagger him regardless, rendering this Talent worthless even if the stars align.

